        <mxCell id="yU9l7hP_QC29vx_HUS9G-88" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#4ec9b0&quot;&gt;OpenCV Imnage Provider Class&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;I cretaed it using inheritance it has method to convert OpenCV Image to pyside 6, in order to use it on QML&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Also it has a member image class typed object&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="45" y="960" width="225" height="180" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="yU9l7hP_QC29vx_HUS9G-90" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#4ec9b0&quot;&gt;Backend Class&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;It is used as a wrapper and main class&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;it has object references of provider class to complete communcation between QML and Pyside6.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Loads qml file and runs engine.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;By sending object references of python classes, it allows not only QML to use variables,datas coming from python backend side but also make it acces to edit properties&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
